### What about event-time and watermarks?

Event-time is when the event actually happened; processing-time is when the system processes it. Watermarks track event-time progress so the system knows when to finalize a window, allowing bounded lateness for late arrivals.

### How do batch and stream coexist?

Modern architectures run both. Streaming handles real-time reactions while batch handles periodic recomputation. At National Bank of India, a fraud alert fires in seconds on the stream, while overnight a Spark batch job recomputes complete, correct interest totals.

### What should a senior engineer know?

Batch is increasingly understood as a special case of streaming over a bounded source. Engines are converging toward this unified model. The key decision is matching each workload to the right path rather than choosing one paradigm exclusively.
